---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';import AustraliaOfferComparison from '../../components/tools/AustraliaOfferComparison';
const title='Australia casual vs part-time: compare confirmed cash offers';
const description='Compare worked-hour and paid-leave cash over the same 52-week scenario, using separate confirmed rates without assuming a casual loading or leave entitlement.';
const url='https://tools.oiyo.net/en/australia-job-offer-comparison/';
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebApplication',name:title,description,url,inLanguage:'en-AU',applicationCategory:'BusinessApplication',operatingSystem:'All',isAccessibleForFree:true};
---
<Layout title={title} description={description} locale="en" languageTag="en-AU" ogLocale="en_AU" canonicalURL={url}><article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-4 px-4 py-6"><header class="space-y-2"><h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">{title}</h1><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">{description}</p><p class="text-sm font-semibold">Australia · illustrative 52-week gross cash comparison</p></header><section class="space-y-2 rounded-lg border border-border p-3"><h2 class="font-semibold">Check the actual offer and applicable rules first</h2><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">This compares inputs, not employment status, minimum lawful pay or entitlements. No automatic 25% casual loading is added. Enter a confirmed worked-hour cash rate including any applicable loading already quoted, excluding superannuation. Leave is paid at its own confirmed rate; leave loading may differ under an award or agreement.</p><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">Casual employment does not mean no paid leave in every case: paid family and domestic violence leave is one exception. Do not infer your leave hours from a label. This tool does not value job security, non-cash benefits, tax, super, penalties, overtime, public holidays, variable pay or leave accrual. The weekly pattern is an assumption, not guaranteed work or a forecast.</p></section><AustraliaOfferComparison client:load/><section class="space-y-2 border-t border-border pt-4"><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Method and official sources</h2><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">Scenario cash = weekly worked hours × weeks actually worked × confirmed worked-hour cash rate + paid leave hours × confirmed leave rate. Worked hours and paid leave must fit inside weekly hours × 52; unused hours are simply unpaid or unworked time in this scenario. Fifty-two weeks is a comparison window, not an exact calendar-year payroll calculation.</p><ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm"><li><a class="text-primary underline" href="https://www.fairwork.gov.au/starting-employment/types-of-employees/casual-employees">Fair Work: casual employees and leave exceptions</a></li><li><a class="text-primary underline" href="https://www.fairwork.gov.au/starting-employment/types-of-employees/part-time-employees">Fair Work: part-time employment</a></li><li><a class="text-primary underline" href="https://www.fairwork.gov.au/leave/annual-leave/payment-for-annual-leave">Fair Work: payment for annual leave and leave loading</a></li></ul><p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Official guidance checked: 26 October 2026. Individual legal and award assessment is outside this calculator. Inputs are calculated in browser memory and are not added to the URL. Displayed money is rounded to cents, not a payroll rounding instruction.</p></section></article><script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}/></Layout>
